    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i look at my dad and my brother and i just see the same patterns. it’s like it’s all pre-written in the dna or something. no matter how much i try to stay positive or do the therapy stuff, i can feel it just waiting for me. like i’m just a passenger in a body that's eventually gonna break. it feels so useless to even fight it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds incredibly heavy to feel like you're repeating patterns you can't escape, and that feeling of being stuck is exhausting. Acknowledging these inherited tendencies is a significant first step, even if it feels hopeless right now. Remember that while genetics sets a backdrop, your choices and how you respond to those patterns are still uniquely yours to shape. Seeking support to explore these family dynamics in a deeper way might offer new avenues for change.",
