    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's the thing, it doesn't feel like \"choices\" anymore. it feels like a script. like i'm just watching a movie i've already seen a hundred times, and i already know how it ends for people like me. it feels less like a struggle and more like just... waiting for the inevitable. how can i even believe i have \"agency\" when the biology is already decided?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When things feel scripted, it's natural to feel powerless, as biology certainly plays a huge role in our predispositions. However, agency doesn't always mean rewriting the entire script; sometimes it means choosing how you react to the lines in front of you. Even small deviations—a different response to stress or a moment of self-compassion—are real choices that build a different narrative. Therapy can help you identify those tiny points where the \"passenger\" can actually start to steer the vehicle.",
      "source": "target",
